# Single responsibility

- Members and types are **private unless a caller outside the type needs them**.
- One type, one job. A `TypeConverter` converts. It is not a helper, registry, or column catalog.
- Loose coupling. Do not add wrapper types, god maps, or public surface “for convenience.”

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — helper API on a converter
public Value Cell(string key, Value value, bool reverse = false) => ...
public static IReadOnlyList<string> Columns => ...

// ✅ GOOD — convert only
public override T Convert(Row from) => ...
public override Row ReverseConvert(T to) => ...
```
